			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2354100">
									

<p>I don't think I've seen a cross-link like this before, but it's very effective and adds a lot of interest to the cross-linked SCP without trying to reimagine it.</p>
<p>It has certain flaws (the vocal cords part is definitely stretching credibility), but overall it's really quite solid - even the (conceptual) weakness of Krupin's anomaly makes sense, given that it's crude, blatant DIY memetics designed only to get him locked up. Krupin's a weird, unlikable asshole, but his characterisation as such is strong. I very much enjoy the fact that you wrote a story about a Foundation researcher carving kill-symbols into their skin without the researcher actually &quot;going crazy&quot; in the stereotypical horror sense.</p>
<p>+1. I'd definitely be interested in seeing more stories like this.</p>

